    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d1050">

                <pb facs="0898" n="782" sameAs="frus:frus1912/pg782"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">File No. 812.113/388.</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Acting Secretary of State
                        to the President</hi>.</head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Department of State</hi>, <lb/>
                            <hi rendition="#italic">Washington</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1912-04-13">
                            <hi rendition="#italic">April 13, 1912</hi></date>.</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>
                    <hi rendition="#small-caps">My Dear Mr. President</hi>: I have the honor to
                    transmit herewith, for your information, a copy of a letter dated April 11 from
                    the Attorney General requesting that, in the future, this Department <pb
                        facs="0899" n="783" xml:id="pg783"/> handle the correspondence relating to
                    exceptions from the prohibition of your proclamation of March 14, 1912, of
                    shipments to Mexico of dynamite for industrial purposes.</p>
                <p>I also have the honor to inclose a copy of the reply which this Department is
                    making to the Attorney General to-day.</p>
                <p>This Department is entirely willing to handle this matter and to prepare the
                    correspondence relating to individual exceptions of shipments of dynamite that
                    has heretofore been prepared by the Attorney General, provided this arrangement
                    meets with your approval.</p>
                <p>I have [etc.]</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Huntington Wilson</hi>.</signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
